# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file to my-test.txt  (cp my-test.txt.example my-test.txt)
#   2. Edit the description below — keep or remove step numbers as you like
#   3. Set test_name and page_paths (both optional but recommended)
#   4. Run:  npm run generate -- --file my-test.txt
#
# my-test.txt is gitignored — it is your local scratchpad and is never committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# test_name:  sets the output file name  →  tests/<test_name>.spec.ts
# page_paths: comma-separated paths the generator will inspect for real locators
#             leave blank to skip live inspection (locators inferred from context)
#
# TIPS
#   • Use () for implementation hints that are not test steps — the AI reads
#     them as guidance, not as assertions:
#       3. Verify the home page loaded (also check the carousel — update verifyLoaded())
#   • If a spec or POM for this feature already exists the AI will ADD to it,
#     not create a duplicate file
#   • Remove # test_name / # page_paths lines if you don't need them
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# test_name: login
# page_paths: /login

Test the login flow on automationexercise.com:

1. Launch browser
2. Navigate to url 'http://automationexercise.com'
3. Verify that the home page is visible successfully
4. Click on 'Signup / Login' button
5. Verify 'Login to your account' heading is visible
6. Enter a valid email address and password
   (use the API to create a test account first via POST /api/createAccount,
    then log in with those credentials — delete the account in afterEach)
7. Click the 'Login' button
8. Verify that 'Logged in as <username>' is visible in the navigation
